<title>FRANCE: EU weighs 12-Ecu wheat refund for some poor states.</title>
<headline>EU weighs 12-Ecu wheat refund for some poor states.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union grain officials were on Thursday considering a new preferential wheat export quota for several developing countries at a fixed refund of 12 Ecus per tonne -- about five Ecus per tonne above the latest ordinary wheat export refund, grain industry sources said.</p>
<p>Weekly grain talks now finishing in Brussels may come up with a move to fix the refund of 12 Ecus per tonne up to the end of the year, they said. A further seven Ecus, applied through a positive corrective, would bring the refund to 19 Ecus from January onwards. A special tender giving preferential but floating refunds to African and other states is about to end.</p>
</text>
